cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these models or the verification layer, please cite them as below."
title: "Single-layer graphene device models: contacts, interconnects and photodetectors, with an explicit verification layer"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gururani
    given-names: Harsh Vardhan
    affiliation: "Department of Physics, Indian Institute of Technology (BHU) Varanasi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/prometheus5863/single-layer-graphene-structure"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-16"
abstract: >-
  Compact, analytical device models of single-layer graphene (back-gated FET
  and metal contacts, interconnect resistivity versus linewidth, two-contact
  photodetectors), validated against exactly known limits and published data,
  together with the audit scripts that check them. Not DFT or NEGF. Developed
  as the computational part of an M.Tech thesis; parts of the code and text
  were drafted with an AI assistant (Claude, Anthropic) under the author's
  direction and review.
keywords:
  - graphene
  - compact model
  - contact resistance
  - photodetector
  - interconnect
  - verification
